1
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,614
Every time you ask an AI a question, something

2
00:00:08,614 --> 00:00:09,765
physical happens.

3
00:00:09,765 --> 00:00:12,879
Somewhere, thousands of servers light up, draw

4
00:00:12,879 --> 00:00:14,572
electricity, and get hot.

5
00:00:14,572 --> 00:00:16,264
AI is changing the world.

6
00:00:16,264 --> 00:00:20,056
But can we build its infrastructure without compromising

7
00:00:20,056 --> 00:00:21,748
the future of our planet?

8
00:00:23,348 --> 00:00:26,074
I'm exploring an answer in Southeast England,

9
00:00:26,074 --> 00:00:28,315
starting with Didcot, in Oxfordshire.

10
00:00:28,315 --> 00:00:31,344
Not a windowless box that consumes power and dumps

11
00:00:31,344 --> 00:00:34,191
heat, but a clean-energy campus, where advanced

12
00:00:34,191 --> 00:00:37,099
computing and the natural landscape are designed

13
00:00:37,099 --> 00:00:38,492
together, from day one.

14
00:00:41,348 --> 00:00:43,355
It starts with the electricity.

15
00:00:43,355 --> 00:00:46,397
New solar and wind, built alongside the campus,

16
00:00:46,397 --> 00:00:48,081
feed the servers directly.

17
00:00:48,081 --> 00:00:50,605
Large battery storage smooths the gaps:

18
00:00:50,605 --> 00:00:53,583
charging when the wind blows, and giving power

19
00:00:53,583 --> 00:00:56,108
back to the grid when it's needed most.

20
00:00:57,708 --> 00:00:59,071
Inside is the engine.

21
00:00:59,071 --> 00:01:02,511
Rows of servers running AI models, each one producing

22
00:01:02,511 --> 00:01:02,835
heat.

23
00:01:02,835 --> 00:01:05,951
Instead of blowing cold air around, liquid flows

24
00:01:05,951 --> 00:01:09,001
in a closed loop right past the chips, carrying

25
00:01:09,001 --> 00:01:12,052
heat to exchangers, and using a fraction of the

26
00:01:12,052 --> 00:01:14,388
water of a conventional data centre.

27
00:01:15,988 --> 00:01:18,557
And that heat doesn't have to be wasted.

28
00:01:18,557 --> 00:01:21,640
Heat pumps can upgrade it, and underground pipes

29
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:24,852
carry it into a local heat network, warming nearby

30
00:01:24,852 --> 00:01:27,357
homes, offices and community buildings.

31
00:01:27,357 --> 00:01:30,247
The by-product of computing becomes something

32
00:01:30,247 --> 00:01:31,660
a town actually needs.

33
00:01:33,988 --> 00:01:37,133
Sustainability has to run through the whole project:

34
00:01:37,133 --> 00:01:40,097
low-carbon materials, modular construction, green

35
00:01:40,097 --> 00:01:42,820
roofs, native planting and restored wetlands,

36
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:45,844
so the site gives back more habitat than it takes.

37
00:01:47,444 --> 00:01:50,192
This is an early concept, and there's serious

38
00:01:50,192 --> 00:01:52,574
engineering and feasibility work ahead.

39
00:01:52,574 --> 00:01:55,689
But I believe the future of artificial intelligence

40
00:01:55,689 --> 00:01:58,376
shouldn't come at the expense of the planet.

41
00:01:58,376 --> 00:02:01,002
We have a chance to build something better.

42
00:02:01,002 --> 00:02:02,468
Let's build it together.

